  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "A language class has $63$ students, $43$ of them are studying English, and $25$ of them are studying Spanish. There are $10$ students studying both languages.\n\nIf $A$ represents the event that a student is studying English, and $B$ represents the event that a student is studying Spanish, which of the following gives the correct Venn diagram for the corresponding sample space?",
